[0.200, "o", "\r\nPerforming Global Updates\r\n(Could take a couple of minutes if you have a lot of binary packages.)\r\n  .='update pass'  *='binary update'  #='/var/db update'  @='/var/db move'\r\n  s='/var/db SLOT move'  %='binary move'  S='binary SLOT move'\r\n  p='update /etc/portage/package.*'\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "/home/vivo/repo/PORTUALE/pmtest/fixtures/repo/profiles/updates/2Q-2024..\r\nERROR: Update type not recognized '# Quarter 2 2024 package moves (fixture)'\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n\r\n"]
[0.045, "o", "\u001b]0;portuale: emerge\u0007"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mAlways study the list of packages to be cleaned for any obvious\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mmistakes. Packages that are part of the world set will always\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mbe kept.  They can be manually added to this set with\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[32;01m`emerge --noreplace <atom>`\u001b[39;49;00m.  Packages that are listed in\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mpackage.provided (see portage(5)) will be removed by\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mdepclean, even if they are part of the world set.\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mAs a safety measure, depclean will not remove any packages\r\n\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00munless *all* required dependencies have been resolved.  As a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00mconsequence of this, it often becomes necessary to run \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[33;01m * \u001b[39;49;00m\u001b[32;01m`emerge --update --newuse --deep @world`\u001b[39;49;00m prior to depclean.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\nCalculating dependencies "]
